-- chemistry-knowledge-graph (2026-11-17, Avik, 17:31 PST): "I'm literally interested not in synthesizing
-- dmt but building a chemistry knowledge graph for medicine research"; (17:35 PST, on this direction against
-- his others) "this is good stuff for the chem field right? I have undervalued that direction past month but
-- it may be the most valuable one". The construction is docs/chemical-identity.md.
-- The field's central unsolved problem is chemical entity resolution — deciding when two records are the
-- same substance — and it is the identity crisis of §10.8: digest equality, definitional equality and SemEq
-- are three statements (10.22), and chemistry collapses them into string equality of a canonical identifier.
-- The collapse is documented by the body that maintains the identifier: InChI was intended from the early
-- 2000s to be tautomer-invariant and implements that invariance only partially, IUPAC project
-- #2012-023-2-800 has been open since 2012 to redesign it, and standard InChI's success rate over the
-- tautomeric part of the Cambridge Structural Database is 26.25% (strict 13.46%).
-- What the construction holds: molecules as structured graphs keeping their automorphisms (§4.2, §8.3)
-- rather than the set quotient, because the automorphism group order is the symmetry number σ in the
-- rotational partition function and therefore a term in the entropy; chirality as an orientation component
-- that identity has to commute with, so a meso compound is the case where the inverting map lies in the
-- automorphism group; tautomers as a higher inductive type whose paths are the proton transfers, so a
-- property either respects them and descends or has to supply the ensemble; affinities as witness-carrying
-- relations (2.10) and assay readings as observations whose fiber says what they warrant (1.3); computed
-- quantities with dependency certificates (10.17), so one corrected measurement invalidates exactly its
-- dependents (10.25); reactions as transitions with the mechanism as witness (3.11), with mass balance as
-- the conservation invariant (§10.3) and the atom-atom map part of the witness; Markush patent claims as
-- dependent types, where infringement is inhabitation.
-- Two public results to produce, each checkable by anyone and unobtainable from the standard
-- representation: automorphism-orbit counts predict the number of distinct ¹H and ¹³C NMR signals, checked
-- against published spectra at scale; and retraction propagation — take a documented bad measurement, find
-- its dependents, show which conclusions lose their warrant and which survive, which nobody in chemistry
-- can currently answer for any retraction.
-- Crystallography before medicinal chemistry: crystallography never took the set quotient (unit cell plus
-- space group, Wyckoff positions as orbits of the space-group action, the 230 space groups as the finite
-- classification of the structured-equivalence data), the symmetry data is already in the experimental
-- record, polymorphism has a documented eight-figure cost (ritonavir, Form II in 1998, withdrawal and
-- reformulation, more than US$250 million), and the identity half needs no collaboration. The measurement
-- half needs people who run assays to state what their readouts warrant, and that is the slower half.
-- The substance nodes of docs/preventable-death-at-scale.md stand on this: each carries a receptor, a
-- mechanism and a measured affinity, and its links lines are typed edges written in prose because the typed
-- object did not exist.
-- The document's record as of 2026-11-18, each figure from the field's own publications: InChI was intended
-- to be tautomer-invariant and implements that only partially (standard InChI's success rate over the
-- tautomeric part of the CSD is 26.25%, strict 13.46%; IUPAC #2012-023-2-800 open since 2012). Krotko
-- (2020) reports Ivanciuc's conclusion that only algorithms determining the graph automorphisms explicitly
-- can get all symmetry classes right; O'Boyle (2012) that no standard exists for canonical SMILES, that
-- CANGEN never treated stereochemistry, that parts are trade secret, and that each toolkit therefore
-- generates its own; and the field's own structural objection, that identifying two graphs as isomorphic
-- does not give a unique identifier, which is 8.3's argument verbatim. Grohe and Schweitzer trace color
-- refinement, the basic subroutine of practical isomorphism testing, to Morgan's 1965 algorithm for
-- Chemical Abstracts Service, so chemistry invented the subroutine and discards the automorphism group it
-- computes on the way to the label: keeping the group is not an added cost. The InChIKey's designers
-- publish its collision rate (1.3% for a first-block collision at one billion compounds, 0.014% at one
-- hundred million), which is the first clause of (10.22) with an error bar. Identity in practice is an
-- authority: the CAS Registry, started 1965, hundred-millionth substance on 30 June 2015, numbers
-- copyright CAS/ACS with compiling substantial lists forbidden, about half a percent of it open — the
-- closed half of Murray-Rust's complaint that no authority assigns open identifiers, and the same object as
-- data-liberation. Marsh's survey found 279 of about 1,300 CSD structures in P1 wrongly assigned, 157 of
-- them because the overline was missing from P1-bar; in the wrong space groups bond lengths and angles are
-- severely distorted and become normal on revision, so the symmetry data is what makes the chemistry
-- right, and Raymond and Girolami add that incorrect structures often have good R values. AFLOW, the
-- Materials Project and OQMD differ by up to 0.105 eV/atom in formation energy computed from the same
-- input structure, the peak disagreement traced to a chosen elemental reference, and Kirklin's 1,670
-- experimental comparisons give a 0.096 eV/atom error against experiments that disagree with each other by
-- 0.082. Lowe's patent corpus has no standard filter for erroneous records, a substantial atom- and
-- charge-unbalanced fraction, and machine-generated atom maps; 720,768 duplicates were removed by comparing
-- strings with the mapping stripped, which is the digest relation standing in for chemical identity.
-- Twilight holds 2,815 PDB complexes with ligand RSCC below 0.6, and 29.2% of 382,588 ligands have
-- partially missing density, with the crystallographers' own rule that strong claims require
-- correspondingly strong evidence. Docking: 59.8% top-scored pose accuracy, 20-40% on non-cognate
-- structures, protein conformation not among the searched degrees of freedom. And Scannell's October 2025
-- diagnosis that the core problem is the collapse of predictive validity in preclinical models, which is
-- Warrants(y,P) reached from the economics.
-- Where the graph model ends: InChI disconnects metal bonds, which the field says makes most inorganic
-- InChIs meaningless, and IUPAC 2009-040-2-800 has been open since November 2010. Delocalized multi-centric
-- bonding is not a four-bond-type graph, so there identity is not graph identity and the carrier itself has
-- to be a definition.
-- The construction (2026-11-18, chem/identity.cub): Mol is the molecule as the structured graph of its
-- atoms — a type of atoms, each atom's element, each ordered pair's bond — so no numbering of the atoms
-- is part of the molecule. Auto is an automorphism, carrying its inverse as data and its preservation of
-- element and bond; auto-id, auto-comp and auto-inv are its group structure, each proved. Orbit is the
-- witnessed same-orbit relation with orbit-refl, orbit-sym and orbit-trans, and orbit-invariant is the
-- theorem the field states informally and cannot enforce: an observation of an atom invariant under the
-- automorphisms is constant on orbits, which is what makes chemically equivalent positions a property of
-- the molecule and not of a drawing. Taut carries the tautomers as a type whose paths are the proton
-- transfers, and taut-respects says that any function out of it already respects every transfer, so a
-- tautomer-dependent quantity cannot be stated of the substance at all. digest-sound is all that any
-- hashing scheme establishes; DigestInjective is what would license reading identity off a string;
-- Collision is two molecules not identical whose digests are, and collision-not-injective refutes
-- injectivity from a single one. Hand, Oriented, or-mirror, Meso and meso-self-mirror put chirality
-- beside the graph, where a meso compound's relabelling-invariant observations read the same on it and on
-- its mirror image. OrAuto, OrOrbit and or-orbit-refines add the automorphisms of the oriented molecule
-- and prove that their orbits refine the graph's, which is the homotopic-versus-diastereotopic
-- distinction as a statement about groups and says what the NMR demonstration must be. AtomMap is mass
-- balance without counting, with am-after-auto and am-before-auto giving both automorphism groups'
-- action on the atom maps, so a stored map is a representative of an orbit with the orbit discarded.
-- Scope and scope-respects make a claim's coverage a type family that cannot distinguish identical
-- molecules. Solid, PolymorphPair and polymorph-not-determined separate the solid's identity from the
-- molecule's by refutation from one published pair (ritonavir Form II); Substance, ProvenanceCollision
-- and provenance-not-identity separate the substance's from its provenance the same way. NonTransitive
-- and non-transitive-not-identity carry the biologics regime: a reflexive relation with one failure to
-- compose cannot be read as identity, however many pairwise comparisons to the reference hold. Report
-- holds a measurement with the proposition it rests on as a type and an inhabitant of it, Derived holds
-- the reports a quantity was computed from, and der-retracted proves that refuting one warrant refutes
-- the quantity, with nothing recomputed and nothing marked stale. Measured, Distinct, DoubleCount and
-- double-count-not-distinct give the measurement event its own identity, which is what the ChEMBL
-- uncertainty analysis had to establish by hand before it could estimate anything: 90% of the pairs it
-- examined were one measurement cited twice. BindClaim and bind-transport are the pharmacology layer, a
-- claim about an oriented molecule carried along identity and along nothing else. Interconv, ic-within
-- and the thalidomide instance (td-inv, td-one-in-a-day, td-two-in-ten-minutes) make the identification
-- of forms depend on the observation window, computed from the measured serum half-lives: over a day the
-- two enantiomers are one, over ten minutes they are two, which is why resolving them would not have
-- prevented the harm. NonTransitiveAt and non-transitive-at-not-identity carry both regimes that rest on
-- similarity -- the biosimilar, which under-licenses, and the Analogue Act, which over-licenses a
-- criminal liability. BScope, AffinitySettles, Evasion and evasion-refutes refute the control instrument:
-- a structural class cannot settle what it was imposed to settle, and each generation of the unregulated
-- supply is one molecule outside the class with the action inside it. vacuous-report, Informative and
-- unit-warrant-not-informative say what a warrant is worth: a report can always be made, so the existence
-- of a record is no evidence, and a family of warrants is informative exactly when some claim is refused.
-- The worked case, at-h-one-orbit and at-h-not-one-or-orbit, proves both halves of the NMR statement on
-- one molecule, and at-map-id, at-map-swap and at-maps-differ prove two distinct atom maps for one
-- reaction, so a stored map is a choice out of an orbit of two. ic-respects joins the interconversion
-- data to the tautomer carrier. 313 definitions check.
-- The next construction step, named exactly (2026-11-18): the enantiotopic case, where the correct signal
-- count depends on the medium. It needs a modelling change and not another theorem. Handedness as this
-- module has it is a value at each atom, which is enough to separate the worked pair but not to derive
-- diastereotopicity in general: in a CH2 adjacent to a stereocentre nothing combinatorial distinguishes
-- the two hydrogens, and what distinguishes them is the parity of the local tetrahedral arrangement at
-- their own carbon, together with the configuration at the centre. So the stereo datum has to be a parity
-- on each tetrahedral atom's neighbours, with an automorphism required to preserve it; then the swap of
-- the two hydrogens reverses a parity and is not an automorphism of the stereo structure, which is
-- diastereotopicity derived rather than assigned, and the global mirror reverses every parity, so in an
-- achiral medium the swap composed with the mirror is an automorphism and the pair is identified again --
-- three groups, three verdicts on one molecule, the medium deciding which applies. What this needs first
-- is less than it first looks, and the route is worked out here so that whoever writes it does not have
-- to find it again. General permutation parity on four neighbours is not needed. Take the arrangement at
-- a tetrahedral atom to be the cyclic order of three of its neighbours seen from the fourth: a type
-- Cyc A whose points are triples and whose paths are the three-cycles (the same higher inductive shape as
-- Taut, one path constructor taking (a,b,c) to (b,c,a)). The stereo datum is an element of Cyc for each
-- centre; an automorphism must carry each arrangement to the same element, which is to say the relabelled
-- triple must be a rotation of the original. Then the case comes out by itself: at the CH2 carbon the
-- neighbours are (h1, h2, C*), the swap of the two hydrogens gives (h2, h1, C*), which is not a rotation
-- of (h1, h2, C*), so the swap is not an automorphism of the stereo structure and the two hydrogens are
-- separated -- diastereotopicity derived, not assigned. The mirror reverses every arrangement,
-- (a,b,c) to (a,c,b); the swap composed with the mirror gives (h2, C*, h1), which is a rotation of the
-- original, so in an achiral medium the pair is identified again. The one lemma to prove is a sign on
-- Cyc over a finite atom type that respects the rotation path, by which the two elements above are shown
-- distinct; a three-cycle is even, so the sign is constant on rotations, and the case analysis is over
-- the orderings of three ranks. Declaring the parity as data beside the automorphism would let a false
-- automorphism through, and a construction that can be gamed is not one, which is why it waits for this
-- and not for a convention.
-- One defect of the core found in writing it (2026-11-18): the checker refuses a declaration with three
-- type-valued parameters returning Type 1; two are accepted, and parameters of data types are accepted
-- in any number. Derived computes into its reports' own value type for that reason.
-- What waits on the library: the unchosen enumeration (HasCard, the truncated equivalence with Fin n)
-- and the truncation of Orbit into a proposition. lib/derive.cub's definitions are without signatures,
-- which the checker allows only in the fixed bootstrap files, so lib/library.cub does not check and
-- nothing can be written over it; chem/identity.cub loads after lib/core.cub alone until then. Giving
-- derive.cub's definitions their signatures unblocks every file written over the library, this one
-- included.
chemistry-knowledge-graph : Node
chemistry-knowledge-graph = node "Chemistry is in the knowledge graph at its identity: every molecule, solid, reaction and measurement placed by the relation it actually stands in, and every derived quantity holding the dependencies that govern its reuse." (cons the-product (cons healing-societies nil))
